# neutron-winewayland-decoration
#
# Optional server-side (xdg-decoration) window decorations for winewayland.drv,
# OFF by default. Neutron uses CLIENT-SIDE decorations: Wine draws its own
# non-client frame, themed dark via the prefix's Control Panel colors (see
# neutron-decoration/neutron-premiere-dark.reg). The title bar is then part of the
# window surface, so it is self-contained in the prefix, never overflows onto an
# adjacent monitor, and does not inherit the compositor's global decoration theme
# (KWin has no per-app decoration theme). Set WAYLANDDRV_SSD=1 to opt into
# compositor-drawn frames instead.
#
# When SSD is enabled this implements zxdg_decoration_manager_v1 + the
# pGetWindowStyleMasks driver hook so the compositor draws the frame (v2, or v1
# gated to KDE via HasWindowManager), with the maximize/geometry plumbing that
# server-side frames need. Premiere fights compositor resize/maximize and overflows
# on multi-monitor under SSD, which is why CSD is the Neutron default.
#
# Applies on top of neutron-winewayland-xdg-popup. Touches: Makefile.in,
# xdg-decoration-unstable-v1.xml (new), wayland.c, waylanddrv.h, waylanddrv_main.c,
# window.c, wayland_surface.c.

